          <div class="of-ftype__content">
            <div class="of-ftype__step">02</div>
            <h2 class="of-ftype__title">Anti-Graffiti Film.
Protect. Peel. Replace.</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">Sacrificial anti-graffiti film is a clear protective layer that bonds to glass, stainless steel, mirrors, and architectural metal surfaces throughout transit stations. When tagged or etched, the film is peeled and replaced — not the surface underneath. For stations on high-vandalism corridors, it converts a reactive, unpredictable restoration budget into a predictable maintenance program.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">We have underground SEPTA stations where tagging happens multiple times a week. Is film practical at that frequency?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes — high-frequency vandalism is exactly where sacrificial anti-graffiti film delivers the most value. The film is peeled and replaced rather than requiring glass restoration or etching removal. Replacement is fast, relatively low-cost, and can be performed during off-peak hours without closing the station.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does anti-graffiti film work on the stainless steel and metal surfaces in our stations, not just glass?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes. Sacrificial anti-graffiti film bonds to smooth metal surfaces — stainless steel elevator panels, fare gate housings, column cladding, platform mirrors — as well as glass. The same peel-and-replace approach applies regardless of the surface material.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How does anti-graffiti film hold up to the cleaning chemicals transit agencies use?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Anti-graffiti film is resistant to the cleaning agents commonly used in transit maintenance, including industrial degreasers and pressure washing. The film is designed for high-maintenance environments. We can provide chemical compatibility documentation for your facilities team before installation.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="of-ftype__cta">Get an anti-graffiti estimate →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

