            <h2 class="of-ftype__title">Decorative &amp; Privacy Film.
Operations. Wayfinding. Brand.</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">Frosted <a href="/benefits/decorative-promotional/" style="color:#a5d6a7;font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:#81c784;text-underline-offset:3px;">decorative and privacy film</a> for transit operations centers, ticketing windows, and security glazing — plus printed graphic film for wayfinding, gate identification, and terminal artwork installations. 3M Fasara offers dozens of patterns from subtle linen to bold geometric, matched to your facility's design language.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">We need visual privacy for our operations center windows that overlook the terminal. What are our options?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Frosted decorative and privacy film provides one-way visual privacy during daylight hours — staff inside see out; passengers in the terminal see an opaque surface. 3M Fasara films are available in dozens of patterns from subtle linen to bold geometric, and can be matched to your facility's design language.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can we use film to create wayfinding graphics or branded glass in the terminal?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes. Printed decorative film can carry any graphic, pattern, or brand element and is applied directly to glass. It's used in airports for gate identification graphics, sponsor walls, retail partition branding, and terminal artwork installations. Film removes cleanly when graphics need updating.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Our security operations windows need privacy but our officers need to see the terminal floor clearly. Is there a one-way solution?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>One-way mirror film achieves this during daytime: the reflective exterior side prevents passengers from seeing into the operations room, while officers inside have a clear view of the terminal. Effectiveness depends on maintaining lower light levels inside than outside — standard for most security operations centers.</div>
